WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:03.860
[Jake]: One of the things we do around here at Corridor Crew is give you guys an appreciation

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:09.320
for the art and the craft of filmmaking and part of that appreciation comes from an understanding

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:14.880
So today we're doing the Jackie Chan Olympics. We've done other celebrity Olympics around here in the past

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.740
In fact, Nico holds the title for Office Tom Cruise

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.900
Sam holds the title of Office Indiana Jones

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.020
And today, we compete for the title of Office Jackie Chan!

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.600
fancy logo

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:28.300
Now, with Sam and Nico already holding Office titles,

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.840
we brought in two extra players to help round out the competition

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:35.040
We've got D from Node and we've got Wes, who's an awesome filmmaker and creator

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.840
You may have seen his stuff on Instagram or on Facebook

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:40.060
or you may have caught him right here on the Corridor Cast

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:42.180
[Jake]: I've got a bunch of Jackies around me

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:43.360
(off-camera) Which Jackie are you?

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:46.620
[Clint]: So today I'm coming in with Jackie Chan from "Wheels on Meals"

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:48.540
[D]: I'm Agent Lee from "Rush Hour"

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:50.460
The BEST Jackie Chan movie, in my opinion

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.550
[Jake]: I'm "Rumble in the Bronx" Jackie all the way

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:55.600
[Wes]: (perfect 'Drunken Master' impression) "Drunken Master" Jackie Chan

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:59.160
[Wren]: See, no one's representing older Jackie.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.980
So that's what I am. I'm "The Foreigner".
I'm wizened, old Jackie Chan

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:06.140
[Clint]: I'm so glad that we decided to do this because I'm gonna win this whole thing, guys

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:06.670
*wow*

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:11.680
[Jake]: You hear that confidence? I think there's a lot more competition here today than he realized

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:12.520
myself included

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:15.658
[Wes]: I'm gonna win it for sure. I was raised in Japan

00:01:15.658 --> 00:01:17.120
(off-camera) Really? Yea, I grew up in Okinawa.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:20.880
[Wren and Wes speaking Japanese]

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:26.660
[Jake]: Now, in order to make this Jackie Chan official, we've set up several challenges inspired directly from his movies

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:28.040
Let's Get Started!

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:31.856
The first challenge is a simple Kip-up from the ground onto your feet (off-camera) "simple"

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.120
[Wes]: That's right. "Simple"

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:39.020
Jackie Chan does this- he gets knocked over and he does this perfect, beautiful Kip-up back onto his feet and he keeps fighting

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:40.860
[Nick]: Why is it called Kip-up, not Kick-up?

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:41.360
[Wren] (off-camera) ketchup

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:42.240
[Clint]: I dunno

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:43.500
(people saying "ketchup")

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:45.460
[D]: You're kicking and you're flipping, so it's a Kick-flip

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:45.960
[Nick and D]: It's a Kip

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:47.120
[Wren]: A Kick-flip

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:48.380
[D]: You put it together, equals Kip

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:49.926
A Flick-up, which just sounds not as-

00:01:49.926 --> 00:01:51.180
[Nick]: No, that's not as cool

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:53.110
[Jake]: Each person is only going to get three tries to do this

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:55.760
So the worst person will be eliminated

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:56.820
[D]: Perfect. Perfect.

00:01:56.820 --> 00:02:00.060
[Jake]: Then I think since you were the most hyped about this you got to go first, man.

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:00.740
[Clint]: All right, let's go!

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:01.840
Let's Go!

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:02.400
LET'S GO

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:04.400
[Jake]: (off-camera) And Clint,

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:04.900
THREE

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:05.560
TWO

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:06.100
ONE

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:06.600
GO!

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:08.940
(sounds of shock and awe)

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:10.800
(Clint dusts off hands like it's no big deal)

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:12.200
[D]: That was pretty good! (off camera) Smooth!

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.720
[D]: I didn't think that you were gonna do that THAT well on the first try!

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:15.760
[Wren]: SO SILENT

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:21.640
[D]: That was so easy. It was almost dead silent. That is really good- that was pretty good

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.840
[Wes]: Pretty nice. I think I'm gonna add some sauce to that, though

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:25.380
(off-camera) Wes wants it!

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:26.260
let's see it!

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:27.780
[Wes]: You guys ready for this?

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:28.580
[Jake]: And...

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:29.080
Three...

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:29.960
Two...

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:30.660
One...

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:31.160
Go!

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:32.300
(wig flies off)

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:35.400
(various Woo! sounds)

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:37.980
[Wren]: Dude, he did it so cleanly, he lost his hair!

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:42.220
[D]: Now the three-point landing is pretty clutch, too

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:44.540
[Wren]: Can you do a Kip-up?

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:47.340
[D]: I used to be able to do Kip-ups. I haven't done one in a really long time

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:48.640
[Wren]: Me neither, man!

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:49.660
(sucks teeth in fear)

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:52.920
[Jake]: "Rumble in the Bronx" Jackie. It's all on the line. Let's get this!

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:54.780
(supportive sounds for Jake)

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:55.440
Got my Jackie shoes on

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:57.120
(various) All right, ready?

00:02:57.580 --> 00:02:58.760
(supportive clapping)

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:01.980
(struggled noise)

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:03.500
(supportive groans)

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:04.000
[D]: almost!

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:04.960
[Clint]: There's potential (2x)

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.040
[Wes]: That's a kick-puh (?)

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:07.880
(off-camera) Do a Tri-flip!

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:09.240
Do a Tri-flip

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:14.160
(various sounds of struggle and support)

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:16.600
[Jake]: C'mon!

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:19.520
(c'mon Jackie)

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:23.620
(wig flies off)

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:27.420
(failure)

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:29.380
("NO" in unison)

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:29.960
[Jake]: No!

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:31.200
(sorry, Jake)

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:32.520
[Jake]: Dude...

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:37.400
That's- that's the closest I've probably ever gotten, though. I summoned all of my Jackie Strength

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:40.640
[D]: I feel like I could get it after three. I don't know. It's been a looong time

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:41.560
(rubs hands)

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:42.060
(breathes)

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:43.380
[Jake]: Alright, D, good luck!

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:44.720
(perfect Agent Lee impression) Tucker, wait!

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:46.340
(Sci-fi sound)

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:47.720
(probably Wren) aieeee

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:48.280
(probably Clint) ohfff

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:49.100
(applause and wooos)

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:54.620
(more applause)

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:56.020
[Wren]: !!!

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:59.400
[D]:I did it! That was- not very clean, but I did it

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:03.260
[Wren] (worried) Oh man! I'm in trouble!

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:05.860
[Jake]: All right, Wren, good luck. It's between me and you, man.

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:07.000
Whoever does it worse!

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.960
I'm hoping old man Jackie doesn't have what he used to have

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:13.080
(strike one)

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:14.600
[D]: Close!

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:17.880
Wren, Wren- all you gotta do is when you go back you gotta

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:21.800
POP your front forward. Roll onto that and then, when you do it, SNAP that forward

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:24.400
(strike two)

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:25.900
(supportive laughter)

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:30.280
[Clint]: Wr- Wre- Wren, see it in your head and then be like, "I can do it!" and then you do i-

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:31.120
[Wren]: THAT'S WHAT I'M DOING!!!

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:32.040
[D]: Here it goes

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:34.940
(strike three)

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:37.080
(strike four)

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:38.540
(five)

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:39.940
(six)

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:42.660
(Wren ejecting himself from the competition)

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:44.800
[Wes]: Where you going???

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:46.200
(ten)

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:48.340
[D]: Wren ejected himself from the competition

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:48.840
[Clint]: *BOINNNG*

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:52.620
[Wes]: Wren is out there. He's in Studio City now. I don't see him anymore

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:54.680
[D]: Some say he's still trying to Kip-up

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:57.740
[Jake]: I'll take it, man. I'll take it. Let's move on to the next challenge

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:59.580
[Clint]: Alright. So in most Jackie Chan movies,

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:04.220
you'll see Jackie running up a wall and grabbing a high ledge in order to escape the bad guys

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:06.020
or maybe as a diversion through a chase scene

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:07.780
So that's what we're doing here today. We're at this wall

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:12.010
We're gonna grab some yellow gaff, wall run up this thing, slap a piece at the top. Whoever gets the highest wins

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:17.000
We're also taking into account number of steps on the wall. And, of course, style points because it is a Jackie Chan competition

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:18.120
[Wes]: Ready?

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:20.460
Be One With The Wall

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:21.340
Here we go!

00:05:23.560 --> 00:05:24.060
(HAH)

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:25.460
(various whoas)

00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:26.280
[D]: That was high!

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:27.860
[Wren]: Dude, that was really good!!!

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.780
[D]: You almost hit the grain

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:34.560
[Clint]: That's pretty good, man

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:37.000
[Wren]: Okay, now, TECHNICALLY that's only half stuck up there

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:37.560
[Clint]: nah, it- it's-

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:39.220
(anxious laughter)

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:41.840
[Jake]: Looks like it's 125 and a half (feet?)

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:43.120
[Wes]: yessssssss

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:43.620
[Jake]: I'll give it a shot.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:50.000
[Clint]: Little-known fact: Jake's name does start with a J, the same letter in Jackie's first name. So...

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:54.300
(slap)

00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:55.860
[D]:Pretty good, pretty good

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:57.220
[Clint]: That was really close!

00:05:57.920 --> 00:05:59.820
[Jake]: That's not bad. I'll take it!

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:00.820
I'll take it

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:03.180
That's 120 and a half.

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:05.000
[D]: I was not expecting Jake to do that well

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:05.594
alrightalrightalright

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:07.100
[Jackie J]: Jackie, Good luck

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:08.340
[Jackie D]: Thank You, Jackie

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:11.100
(bangs knee into wall)

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:14.860
(off-camera) Valient Effort!

00:06:14.860 --> 00:06:15.840
[D]: Ooh, I banged my knee again...

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:18.460
daaang

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:19.480
(sympathetic applause)

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:21.100
[Jake]: Let's get an opinion on that, guys

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:23.339
[D]: I SMACKED my knee into the wall again

00:06:23.339 --> 00:06:24.236
[Jackie C]: Is Jackie okay?

00:06:24.236 --> 00:06:25.020
[Jackie D]: Yeah. Jackie's alright

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:32.309
[Jake]: 119 and a half. So far, Wes is in first with 125 and a half. I'm in second with 120 and a half

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:37.540
D's in third with 119 and a half. We'll see how Clint fares. It's all up to him now

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:38.040
[Clint]: I'm goin' to the top

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:38.540
heh

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:39.300
(Clint psyching himself up)

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:42.680
(slap)

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:45.420
[All]: OHHHHHHH

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:47.160
(successful applause)

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:47.800
WOW

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:54.100
[Wren]: DUDE

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:57.180
I think Clint was definitely the winner here. Sorry- Jackie (C) was the winner here

00:06:57.250 --> 00:07:01.260
Jackie (W) was second place and Jackie (J) was third place and Jackie (D) was fourth place

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:05.600
Jackie (D) also lost. Sorry, Jackie. At least you have a good retirement with the force

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:06.600
(sighs in defeat)

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:12.500
[Jake]: But, we have you guys as judges and what better than to have the two oldest Jackies being the judges with all that wisdom

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:13.940
Let's move on

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.320
[D]: That is so good!

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:16.980
Dude, this was such a good show

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:18.100
[Clint]: I know. It was the best!

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:19.300
[Uncle]: JACKIEEE

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:21.500
You dishonor your Uncle!

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:24.620
[Clint]: We were just doing some research on different Jackie Chan challenges

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:29.360
and we realized that Jackie is always very, very close with his uncle, no matter if it's the animated show

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:30.380
or if it's "Rumble the Bronx"

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:31.980
[D]: He's constantly yelling out "Uncle!"

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:32.920
[Keung]: Uncle!

00:07:32.920 --> 00:07:33.420
Uncle!!!

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:33.920
[Uncle]: ...

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:34.420
[Keung]: UNCLE

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:36.340
UNCLEEEEEEE

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:39.120
[Clint]: ...and I figured that is a great leg up for me, because,

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:42.420
I bet you, out of everyone here in the office, I'm closest with my uncle.

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:44.900
[D]: I haven't talked to my uncle in years. I don't even know if he's still alive

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:45.500
[Clint]: How close are you with your uncle?

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:47.780
[Wes]: I just talked to my uncle yesterday.

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:48.900
[Clint]: How close are you with your uncle?

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:50.400
[Wren]: (proudly) I'm very close with my UncleS

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:53.620
[Clint]: Look, guys. I can guarantee. I am THE closest with my uncle

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:54.480
[Wes]: Call him right now

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:55.720
[Clint]: First ring. First ring

00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:56.220
[Wes]: Put him on speakerphone

00:07:56.220 --> 00:07:56.720
[Wren]: Really?!

00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:57.560
[Wren]: Uncle Jack...?

00:07:58.400 --> 00:07:59.000
(first ring...)

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:00.180
[Clint]: Uncle Jack...

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:00.860
[Clint]: He usually picks u-

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:01.520
[Uncle Jack]: HEY. CLINT.

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:02.500
[D]: Wow. One ring

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:04.220
[Clint]: Uncle Jack, what's up, man!

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:05.680
It's bee- been uhhh

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:06.540
I guess since yesterday...

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:08.000
[Uncle Jack]: WHAT'S GOING ON IN THE STUDIO THERE TODAY???

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:11.209
We're just here doing like a Jackie Chan challenge that reminded me-

00:08:11.209 --> 00:08:11.920
I'll give you a call

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:12.640
[Uncle Jackie]: OHHH

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:14.060
RIGH RIGHT THAT'S GREAT YEAH YEAH

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:14.560
ANYWAYS

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:15.740
LONG AS WE'RE ON THE SUBJECT OF THE VIDEOS

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:16.240
UM

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:17.640
YOUR MOM WANTED ME TO TELL YOU

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:19.520
TO TELL THE AUDIENCE ABOUT TODAY'S SPONSOR:

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:22.220
DID YOU DO THAT YET?

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:23.400
[Clint]: How do you know about today's sponsor?

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:25.800
[Uncle Jack]: That it's a brand new, free-to-play RPG

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:30.560
taking the mobile gaming landscape by storm! 
It's got almost 10 million players worldwide

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:31.060
AND

00:08:31.060 --> 00:08:34.900
you got over 400 champions. You can gather orcs, undead, night elves and more

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:39.259
I mean, I've been playing a crap-ton of this game.
It's been fantastic!

00:08:39.260 --> 00:08:44.340
I mean you can assemble teams and play as factions. You can enjoy a fully-voiced-over story campaign

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:50.020
I mean, it's just lovely. But don't take my word for it- They've got over 200,000 reviews- all positive, of course!

00:08:50.020 --> 00:08:51.680
[D]: Clint, there is no way that's your uncle!

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:52.840
[Uncle Jack]: WHAT YOU THINK ABOUT THAT?

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:55.760
[Clint]: I just think that's very odd and very specific

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:59.780
[Uncle Jack]: I didn't talk to Jake or anything but he said, "Go to the description of this video,

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:05.380
Click the links and for people that are new, they'll get 50,000 silver and a free epic champion to start"

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:07.500
HEY, HAVE FUN WITH YOUR JACKIE CHAN THING, MAN

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:11.060
[Clint]: Uh- real quick, just one last question for you. Where are you right now?

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:11.820
[Uncle Jack?]: UHHH

00:09:12.140 --> 00:09:12.640
UMMM

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:13.660
I'M UHHH

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:14.740
IN MY LOUNGE

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:15.300
...

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:15.900
[Clint]: alright

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:16.540
bye, uncle

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:18.240
[Probably not Uncle Jack]: Click the link in the description (dial tone)

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:20.960
[Clint]: You guys heard it- Raid: Shadow Legends 
Download it. It's a good time

